sysbar (1.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Command palette: a window opened with a global hotkey that fuzzy-searches
    commands, quick toggles, scenes, clipboard entries, shelf items and audio
    devices. Clipboard entries that look like a secret are masked. Off by
    default.
  * User-defined scenes: scenes can be created, edited and deleted from the
    Scenes window, not just the three built-in presets. A scene is a list of
    typed actions, stored in a JSON manifest under
    ~/.local/share/sysbar/scenes/manifest.json.
  * Scene triggers: a scene can activate on an external monitor being connected
    or on the power/battery level, without overriding a scene chosen by hand.
    Off by default.
  * Command line and D-Bus control: "sysbar <action>" forwards any of the 15
    actions to the running instance; "sysbar --list-actions" prints the catalog.
  * Fix: the Scenes submenu kept a fixed row count, so the menu host no longer
    desynchronizes item state as the number of scenes changes.
  * Fix: an unreadable scenes manifest is moved aside instead of being silently
    overwritten, and a settings-key action that failed to write is no longer
    reported as applied.
  * Fix: Sysbar starts even when the window source used by auto-quit cannot
    subscribe to window events.
  * Fix: the built-in scene names are translated in the Scenes window.

 -- AndreaBonn <andreabonacci95@protonmail.com>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0200

sysbar (1.1.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the panel and settings windows showed GNOME's generic icon in the
    dock and window switcher instead of the Sysbar icon. The window class now
    matches the desktop entry so the branded icon is used.
  * Fix: the About screen, --version, the self-test and the update check
    reported a stale version. The version is now read from the package
    metadata, keeping pyproject.toml the single source of truth.

 -- AndreaBonn <andreabonacci95@protonmail.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 03:18:12 +0200

sysbar (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Tray: show peripheral device batteries (mouse, keyboard, headset and more)
    in the menu, with a settings toggle to hide them.
  * Shelf: open dropped items with the system default application on
    double-click.
  * Branding: ship and register the Sysbar application icon, replacing the
    generic GNOME gear.
  * Italian: translate the remaining tray, scenes, settings and alert strings
    that previously rendered in English.
  * Fix: keep the Scenes submenu from collapsing when opened.
  * Packaging: keep the language directory level when installing locales so
    Italian translations load from the installed package.

 -- AndreaBonn <andreabonacci95@protonmail.com>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 02:49:30 +0200

sysbar (1.0.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Clipboard history manager: searchable, pinnable, persisted; opened from the
    tray and a configurable global hotkey. Off by default (plain-text storage).
  * System monitor: per-metric history sparklines in the panel.
  * System monitor: per-process network throughput section (best-effort via ss).
  * Audio: default output/input device switcher in the panel.
  * Configurable global shortcuts for keep awake, shelf, clipboard and the
    Focus scene.
  * Composable scenes (Focus, Presentation, Power saving) from a tray submenu.
  * CI: GTK window construction smoke tests under xvfb.
  * First stable release.

 -- AndreaBonn <andreabonacci95@protonmail.com>  Sat, 20 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0200

sysbar (0.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Settings: tray metric placement combos for hardware not detected on the
    system (GPU, battery, power) are now disabled with an explanatory
    subtitle, instead of silently showing nothing in the bar or menu.

